# Local runtime data: the search index is generated and can reach ~100 MB.
#
# The contents are excluded rather than the directory itself, because git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded — and one file in here has
# to ship. This host is refused by Sefaria (403), so the corrections below are
# the only thing that can repair the corpus; excluding them would ship a build
# that reports "available: false" and quietly fixes nothing.
apps/api/data/*
!apps/api/data/sefaria-translation-fixes.json
# Anchored to the repository root: unanchored, this matched apps/api/data too.
/data/
apps/api/.env.local

# Android release signing.
#
# A keystore whose password is lost cannot be replaced: Android identifies an update
# by its signing key, so losing this file means unpublishing the app and starting
# again rather than shipping the next version. It is also the single file in this
# repository that would let anyone publish an update to Ilm.
#
# The *fingerprint* in assetlinks.json is derived from it and is public — Android
# has to serve it to verify the link — so that belongs in git and this does not.
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.properties
android/app/*.jks
